1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,448
Please Don't Feed the Ducks.

3
00:00:03,448 --> 00:00:06,167
Ben and I walk around the park pond with Dad.

4
00:00:06,167 --> 00:00:09,000
Ben is carrying the last piece of his sandwich.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,219
When three ducks swim toward us, he starts pulling the bread into little pieces.

6
00:00:13,492 --> 00:00:15,142
Hold on a second.

7
00:00:15,142 --> 00:00:16,965
What does that sign say?

8
00:00:17,236 --> 00:00:19,126
Please don't feed the ducks.

9
00:00:19,126 --> 00:00:21,709
Ben looks at the bread, then at the ducks.

10
00:00:21,709 --> 00:00:24,667
They seem extremely interested in ignoring the sign.

11
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,809
But they came all this way.

12
00:00:26,809 --> 00:00:29,465
It feels rude not to offer them anything.

13
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,952
The park asks visitors to let the ducks find their own food.

14
00:00:32,952 --> 00:00:35,588
We can enjoy watching them without feeding them.

15
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,614
Let's watch them from here.

16
00:00:37,614 --> 00:00:40,343
We sit on a bench a little way back from the water.

17
00:00:40,343 --> 00:00:43,947
Ben keeps his sandwich for himself, and I start counting ducks.

18
00:00:44,212 --> 00:00:46,368
That one looks like it's in a hurry.

19
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:50,873
A small duck paddles past a much bigger one and disappears behind some reeds.

20
00:00:50,873 --> 00:00:52,925
Maybe it's late for duck school.

21
00:00:53,212 --> 00:00:55,985
Or maybe it just knows a good place to look for lunch.

22
00:00:56,212 --> 00:01:00,581
We see one duck shake water off its feathers and another tuck its head down for a rest.

23
00:01:00,581 --> 00:01:04,102
Suddenly, watching them feels more interesting than throwing bread.

24
00:01:04,372 --> 00:01:06,884
The sleepy one is me on Monday morning.

25
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:10,518
On the way out, we put our sandwich wrapper in a trash can.

26
00:01:10,518 --> 00:01:12,425
Ben waves at the pond.

27
00:01:12,425 --> 00:01:16,039
The ducks don't wave back, but one gives a very loud quack.

28
00:01:16,039 --> 00:01:17,904
We decide that counts.
